.TH AGENT-TERMINAL 1 "2026" "agent-terminal" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-terminal \- crash-proof terminal session multiplexer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-terminal new
.RB [ \-s
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR command\ args... ]
.br
.B agent-terminal attach
.B \-s
.I name
.br
.B agent-terminal ls
.br
.B agent-terminal history
.B \-s
.I name
.br
.B agent-terminal kill
.B \-s
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-terminal
keeps long-running terminal programs (AI agents such as Claude Code CLI,
editors, remote shells) alive when the terminal front-end crashes.
A per-user daemon,
.BR agent-terminald (1),
owns the PTY, the emulated screen, and disk-persisted scrollback; the
.B agent-terminal
client merely renders. Killing the client \(em or the entire hosting
terminal application \(em leaves the session running; reattaching restores
the exact screen, cursor, and terminal modes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new
Create a session and attach. Without \fB\-\-\fR, runs \fB$SHELL\fR.
The default session name is \fImain\fR.
.TP
.B attach
Attach to an existing session. Multiple clients may attach; the most
recent attach wins the geometry.
.TP
.B ls
List sessions with size, pid, and client count.
.TP
.B history
Dump a session's scrollback log to stdout (ANSI text; pipe through
.BR less \ \-R ).
Reads the on-disk log directly \(em works with no daemon running and for
dead sessions.
.TP
.B kill
Terminate a session's child process and free the session.
.SH SESSION NAMES
A name becomes a single directory component under
.IR ~/.agent-terminal/sessions/ ,
so it must not contain
.BR / ,
must not begin with
.BR . ,
must contain no control characters, and is capped at 63 bytes. Interior dots
(\fIbuild_2026.08\fR) and non-ASCII names are accepted. An invalid name is
rejected \(em never rewritten \(em and the command exits 1.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl\-\\\\ Ctrl\-d
Detach from the session, leaving it running. A lone
.B Ctrl\-\\\\
is forwarded to the application after a 500 ms timeout.
.SH SSH
Run the system OpenSSH client inside a session:
.IP
.EX
agent-terminal new -s prod -- ssh myhost
.EE
.PP
The child inherits
.I ~/.ssh
configuration and the SSH agent. No SSH or crypto code is implemented by
agent-terminal itself.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/agent-terminal/default.sock
Daemon control socket (0600, peer-UID checked). Falls back to
.IR ~/.agent-terminal/run/ .
.TP
.I ~/.agent-terminal/sessions/<name>/scrollback.log
CRC-framed scrollback log, 2\(mu32 MiB rotation. Survives daemon crashes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR script (1)
